**Key design decisions:**

- `_parse_operands` handles the `--` separator; bare `-` passes through as a filename (length 1 check), any other `-X` before `--` is rejected as unknown option.
- `copy_path` is the semantic anchor: `main` calls it directly for each valid source-dest pair.
- Validation (source exists, is regular file, not self-copy, dest is compatible) happens per-pair before calling `copy_path`, so no destructive change occurs on an invalid pair.
- New files get `src_rwx & ~0o022` via `fchmod`; existing files are opened with `O_TRUNC` only (no `O_CREAT`), preserving their existing rwx.
